metadata/_sms_note = "Pass 150: the Chain Chomp (TBossWanwan), Pianta Village's boss -- a 13 m red-hot Chain Chomp on a 15-link leash. Drop it on flat open ground facing the way it should start (+Z is its mouth); its stake is planted 13 m behind it (or at the PicketPoint node you assign) and it rampages at the end of its chain: it slides and hops along the rail (the Graph node's children IN ORDER are its path; a child with metadata sms_jump = true makes it hop to the next; no Graph = it roams within WanderRadiusUnits), slams down with every bob (the camera shakes within 40 m), and burns you on touch -- the body, and the chain's first eight links while it is hot. Spray it: 255 heat points, 1 a drop (it heals 1 every 20 ticks while hot); as it cools it goes from red through black to a cold blue, at 0 it sits dozing (the cold wait clip) for 20 s before it barks and reheats. COOLED, go to the stake and hold B: you pull it out and the Chomp is loose -- walk backward and the chain drags it along its rail toward you; drag it back past the rail node nearest the BathPoint you assign (the hot spring; a loose Chomp over water with no BathPoint counts too) and it LEAPS into the bath, turns gold over 10 s, and the Shine appears 60 ticks later (ShineScene: assets/ShineSprite.tscn; ShineSpawnPoint or 13 m over it). Grab the stake while it is HOT and it drags YOU around instead. Ground-pound the stake to lock it again (it shakes free after 5 s while hot). Knobs: the level's points (BathPoint, PicketPoint, ShineScene, ShineSpawnPoint), Deviations (SpeedScale, RollSw, JumpSpeedY), Effects (the stomp dust = HipDropLanding scaled x 4, the steam, the splash; the rocks / sparks / heat haze / sparkles are slots), Camera (the two landing shakes), Sounds (ten slots). RelaunchTicks -1 = gone for good."

